---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<Base
  title={`Sudd Library case study | ${site.name}`}
  description="Sudd Library is a free, open-source library of 80+ curriculum resources for South Sudanese teachers and students. Built and deployed by our founder."
  path="/work/sudd-library/"
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case study · Open-source product · Live</p>
      <div class="section-head">
        <h1>Sudd Library</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          A free, open-source library of 80+ curriculum resources for South Sudanese teachers and students: textbooks,
          lesson notes, schemes of work, past papers and holiday packages.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="case-hero">
        <img
          src="/case-studies/sudd-library/homepage.png"
          alt="Sudd Library homepage on a phone, with the library title and search."
          width="720"
          height="1612"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <div class="wrap case-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why it exists</p>
        <h2>Curriculum materials were hard to get</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>
          It was built after volunteering to teach in South Sudan and finding curriculum materials extremely hard to get
          hold of. Many learners, including displaced families, cannot easily reach materials for their own curriculum.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sudd Library closes that gap. It is free to use, with no account, no login and no data collected from the
          people who use it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section case-section-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What it does</p>
        <h2>Organised by level, subject and resource type</h2>
        <p>
          Primary (P1 to P8), Secondary (S1 to S4) and AES, each broken down by subject, then by resource type. Search by
          class, subject or topic, open a resource and download it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="case-shots">
        <figure>
          <img
            src="/case-studies/sudd-library/level.jpg"
            alt="Sudd Library Senior 4 page on a phone, listing 14 subjects grouped as STEM, Languages and Humanities, each with its number of files."
            width="720"
            height="1600"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>A level page: Senior 4, with subjects grouped by area and the number of files in each.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <ul class="case-features">
        <li>
          <h3>Textbooks</h3>
          <p>Linked directly to the National Curriculum Development Centre (NCDC), not re-hosted, because the content is copyrighted.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Lesson notes and schemes of work</h3>
          <p>Prepared from the official NCDC textbooks and syllabus, then checked by a person before publication.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Past papers</h3>
          <p>With marking schemes where they are available.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Holiday packages</h3>
          <p>Packages of materials for the school holidays.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <div class="wrap case-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built to work on weak connections</p>
        <h2>Every resource is a direct link</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>
          Every resource is reachable in a handful of taps. Once a page has loaded, it keeps working on a weak or missing
          connection. On a phone, it can be added to the home screen and opened like an app.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything except textbooks is stored in a public Cloudflare R2 bucket. Textbooks stay on the NCDC's own site.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section case-section-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it is built</p>
        <h2>Free to run, and open for anyone to inspect</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="case-features">
        <li>
          <h3>Astro site, Cloudflare hosting</h3>
          <p>Built with Astro and hosted on Cloudflare Pages and Workers.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Search</h3>
          <p>Pagefind, used to search the resources from the site's own pages.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Content editing</h3>
          <p>A browser-based editor (Decap CMS) commits changes straight to GitHub. Content editors do not need to run anything locally.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Running cost</h3>
          <p>Currently $0 to run.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <div class="wrap case-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Trust and licensing</p>
        <h2>Independent, and clear about what it is not</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>
          Sudd Library is an independent project. It follows the South Sudan national curriculum, but it is not affiliated
          with, endorsed by or run by the NCDC, the Ministry of General Education and Instruction, or any examination
          council.
        </p>
        <p>
          The code is licensed under AGPLv3. The Sudd Library name and logo are reserved, so forks must rename themselves.
          If a resource is wrong, a footer link lets anyone report it, and corrections are made.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section case-section-paper">
    <div class="wrap case-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Where it stands</p>
        <h2>Live and free to use</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>
          Sudd Library is live. It has no fees, no accounts and no adverts. This page does not claim usage numbers, because
          the library does not collect them.
        </p>
        <p>
          It was built and deployed by our founder, Anzuruku Jacob, who designed and built every part of it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <div class="wrap cta-inner">
      <h2>Building something for learners in your community?</h2>
      <p>We reply within {site.replyTime}.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-amber" href="/contact/">Contact us</a>
        <a class="btn btn-light" href="/work/">Back to all work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { margin-top: 0.25rem; }
  .case-hero { margin-top: 2.5rem; display: flex; justify-content: center; }
  .case-hero img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 300px;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.12);
  }
  .case-section { padding: var(--section) 0; }
  .case-section-paper { background: var(--paper); }
  .case-grid { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .case-copy { display: grid; gap: 1rem; max-width: 40rem; }
  .case-features {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
  }
  .case-features li {
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-content: start;
  }
  .case-features p { color: var(--mute); }
  .case-shots { display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .case-shots img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 300px;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.12);
  }
  .case-shots figure { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; justify-items: center; }
  .case-shots figcaption { color: var(--mute); font-size: 0.95rem; text-align: center; max-width: 300px; }
  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .case-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 3rem; align-items: start; }
  }
</style>
